window.docContents[20].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Security.Model/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Security___Model":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Specifications/Security › Model.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the symbolic proof 12 headline theorems depend on it 257 of 403 lines trusted source ↗trust banner in the header: none; the closure computes B2 for the symbolic proofRead the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (46)def IsHandshakeBlockdef HandshakeCompletedAtdef HandshakeKeysAtdef SessionStateExposeddef HandshakeBlocksSecretdef LoggedBeforedef OPKAbsentOrCompromiseddef PQProtectionBypasseddef SameDHKeydef SameOPKdef AliceHandshakeWasCompromiseddef AliceInitiatorSecrecyQuerydef HandshakeAuthWasCompromiseddef ResponderSessionAgreementdef AuthenticationQuerydef BobHandshakeWasCompromiseddef HandshakeWasCompromisedAtdef BobResponderSecrecyQuerydef FSPremisedef ForwardSecrecyQuerydef HNDLPremisedef HNDLQuerydef KCIQuerydef PeerAuthenticationQuerydef SIPremisedef SessionIndependenceQuerydef StateStoredAtdef TRKeyKnowndef HandshakeRootCompromiseddef HonestDHKeydef CompromisedKeydef MessageSeedUseddef FSQuerydef PCSQuerydef AllSecurityQueriesHolddef ForwardSecrecydef PostCompromiseSecuritydef AliceInitiatorSecrecydef BobResponderSecrecydef Authenticationdef PeerAuthenticationdef HandshakeForwardSecrecydef KCIResistancedef SessionIndependencedef HNDLResistancedef AllModelSecurityQueriesHold\n\nSymbolic Security Queries and Reachable-Trace StatementsDefines the ten whole-trace security queries for the composed protocol (FSQuery, PCSQuery, Theorems 7 to 9, and the five Theorem 1 corollaries of Bhargavan et al. and Cheval et al.) and quantifies them over reachable traces of Composed.reachability (AllModelSecurityQueriesHold).\n\n\n\ndef IsHandshakeBlockL52–54 ↗#k is one of the three 32-byte blocks (rk, ck, pqr) of keys.\n\ndef HandshakeCompletedAtL56–60 ↗#AliceDone or BobDone was logged at trace index i with keys.\n\ndef HandshakeKeysAtL62–63 ↗#\n\ndef SessionStateExposedL65–73 ↗#Block k of keys was directly exposed as Triple Ratchet session state (ExposedSpqr for pqr, ExposedCKr / ExposedCKs for ck, or ExposedRK for rk) on a session started by a handshake deriving keys.\n\ndef HandshakeBlocksSecretL75–77 ↗#Every block of keys not exposed via SessionStateExposed is unknown under Knows.\n\ndef LoggedBeforeL79–80 ↗#\n\ndef OPKAbsentOrCompromisedL82–83 ↗#\n\ndef PQProtectionBypassedL85–86 ↗#\n\ndef SameDHKeyL88–90 ↗#Equality of X25519 public keys up to normalizeX25519Key.\n\ndef SameOPKL92–93 ↗#\n\ndef AliceHandshakeWasCompromisedL95–105 ↗#Compromise excuse for Alice's handshake key at i (Bhargavan et al., Theorem 7): either IK_B was compromised (before i, or alongside spk and PQProtectionBypassed), or BrokenDH occurred (before i, or alongside PQProtectionBypassed).\n\ndef AliceInitiatorSecrecyQueryL107–112 ↗#Secrecy of Alice's handshake blocks (Theorem 7).\n\ndef HandshakeAuthWasCompromisedL114–120 ↗#Pre-acceptance authentication compromise excuse at i (Theorem 8): IK_A, Bob's spk, or DH was compromised strictly before i.\n\ndef ResponderSessionAgreementL122–128 ↗#Agreement witness for Theorem 8: a logged AliceDone strictly before i on the same pqpk, spk (up to SameDHKey), and opk (up to SameOPK).\n\ndef AuthenticationQueryL130–134 ↗#Authentication of Alice to Bob (Theorem 8).\n\ndef BobHandshakeWasCompromisedL136–146 ↗#Compromise excuse for Bob's handshake key at i (Theorem 9): pre-acceptance authentication compromise, compromise of all of Bob's session secrets (IK_B, spk, opk, and pqpk/KEM), or BrokenDH paired with PQProtectionBypassed.\n\ndef HandshakeWasCompromisedAtL148–154 ↗#\n\ndef BobResponderSecrecyQueryL156–161 ↗#Secrecy of Bob's handshake blocks (Theorem 9).\n\ndef FSPremiseL163–170 ↗#Premise for handshake forward secrecy at i: identity keys are compromised only after i, session spk and pqpk are uncompromised, and neither DH nor the KEM is broken.\n\ndef ForwardSecrecyQueryL172–177 ↗#Handshake forward secrecy (Theorem 1).\n\ndef HNDLPremiseL179–187 ↗#Premise for harvest-now-decrypt-later resistance at i: BrokenDH occurs only after i, the KEM is unbroken, and ikA, ikB, spk, and pqpk are not explicitly compromised.\n\ndef HNDLQueryL189–194 ↗#Harvest-now-decrypt-later resistance (Theorem 1).\n\ndef KCIQueryL196–202 ↗#Key-compromise-impersonation resistance (Theorem 1).\n\ndef PeerAuthenticationQueryL204–209 ↗#Peer authentication (Theorem 1).\n\ndef SIPremiseL211–220 ↗#Premise for session independence: identity keys, DH, and the KEM are uncompromised, and only prekeys distinct from (spk, pqpk, opk) are compromised.\n\ndef SessionIndependenceQueryL222–227 ↗#Session independence against compromise of other sessions' prekeys (Theorem 1).\n\n\n\ndef StateStoredAtL242–244 ↗#\n\ndef TRKeyKnownL246–249 ↗#Knows holds for either the Double Ratchet seed or the derived hybrid cipher key (trMsgKeys pqSalt seed).cipherKey.\n\ndef HandshakeRootCompromisedL251–255 ↗#k is an initial rk or ck of some PQXDH handshake on tr, and every PQXDH handshake on tr producing k as rk or ck satisfies HandshakeWasCompromisedAt.\n\ndef HonestDHKeyL257–260 ↗#d is an honest DH ratchet secret key on tr (HonestDH or st.dhs of a stored snapshot).\n\ndef CompromisedKeyL262–272 ↗#Ratchet secret k was compromised on tr: directly exposed (ExposedRK, ExposedDHs, ExposedCKs, ExposedCKr, ExposedMK), derived from HandshakeRootCompromised, or an HonestDHKey under BrokenDH (ExposedSpqr excuses no ratchet secret).\n\ndef MessageSeedUsedL274–276 ↗#\n\ndef FSQueryL278–287 ↗#Ratchet forward secrecy (Cheval et al., Table 2): if TRKeyKnown Knows seed pqSalt holds for a used seed, then seed, an ancestor chain key (DerivesMsgKey), or an ancestor root key (DerivesChain) satisfies CompromisedKey.\n\ndef PCSQueryL289–305 ↗#Ratchet post-compromise security (Cheval et al., Table 2): if seed descends from a healing DH step createChain rk_prev (dhPk peerSk) ownSk between honest DH secrets ownSk and peerSk and TRKeyKnown Knows seed pqSalt holds, then seed, a post-heal chain or root key, or both a pre-heal root key and one of (ownSk, peerSk) satisfies CompromisedKey.\n\n\n\ndef AllSecurityQueriesHoldL323–334 ↗#Conjunction of all ten whole-trace security queries on tr against Knows.\n\n\n\ndef ForwardSecrecyL353–354 ↗#\n\ndef PostCompromiseSecurityL356–357 ↗#\n\ndef AliceInitiatorSecrecyL359–361 ↗#\n\ndef BobResponderSecrecyL363–365 ↗#\n\ndef AuthenticationL367–368 ↗#\n\ndef PeerAuthenticationL370–371 ↗#\n\ndef HandshakeForwardSecrecyL373–375 ↗#\n\ndef KCIResistanceL377–378 ↗#\n\ndef SessionIndependenceL380–382 ↗#\n\ndef HNDLResistanceL384–386 ↗#\n\ndef AllModelSecurityQueriesHoldL388–404 ↗#Conjunction of all ten security properties over reachable traces of Composed.reachability.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Specifications/Security/Model.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Security.Model/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Security___Model"}});